# ManaQuest Components

Reuse existing classes. Never duplicate styling — extend.

## Panel (`.panel`)

Wrap any framed surface (hero, character sheet, latest posts, post header, TOC, list pages, taxonomy pages).

```html
<section class="panel panel-loose">
  <header class="section-header">
    <h2>Section Name</h2>
    <span class="section-slot">SLOT&nbsp;LABEL</span>
  </header>
  …content…
</section>
```

- `.panel-loose` adds extra padding when nesting cards inside.
- `.section-slot` always mono uppercase, short (1–2 words or count).

## Button (`.btn` / `.btn-primary`)

Use `.btn-primary` only for the page's main CTA. Everything else is plain `.btn`. Add a leading pixel glyph for game feel: `▶ Play`, `⏵ Watch`, `▣ View`.

## Post card (`.post-card`)

- Always use `.post-card-link` overlay for whole-card click.
- Tag chips inside `.tags` stay on top via z-index 3.
- Add `.has-thumb` class when image present, image rendered via `Resources.GetMatch` (page bundle) with raw URL fallback.

## Code blocks

Handled by render hook `layouts/_default/_markup/render-codeblock.html`. Outputs `<figure class="code-block">` with header (lang + optional title) + line numbers (catppuccin-mocha, inline styles). Don't bypass — write fenced markdown with language.

## Images in prose

Standalone `<img>` inside `<p>` auto-wrapped via `:has()` selector → pixel-corner frame + lightbox click-to-zoom (vanilla JS in `static/js/lightbox.js`). To opt out: `data-no-zoom` attr.

## Gallery shortcode

For multi-image strips:

```md
{{< gallery
  "image-a.png|Caption A"
  "image-b.png|Caption B"
  "image-c.png|Caption C"
>}}
```

Auto-grid 1–4 columns via `data-count`, stacks <720px. Resolves bundle resources first.

## Don'ts

- No new card variants — extend `.post-card` with modifier class.
- No inline `<style>` in templates.
- No new lightbox / no Fancybox / no jQuery.
